<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-all</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:51:25Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-all" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-all" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Indonesia: Flights canceled as Anak Krakatau volcano erupts</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:50b61be1843f974486af152c95e9aea8413a4dfaf9f0941d899ba28849755891</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:51:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T03:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/indonesia-flights-canceled-as-anak-krakatau-volcano-erupts/a-79050871--17392aeed85d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/indonesia-flights-canceled-as-anak-krakatau-volcano-erupts/a-79050871?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The spread of ash after the volcanic eruption of Anak Krakatau has impacted thousands of passengers, as flights were canceled at Jakarta's international airport.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Saxony-Anhalt's state election will have a nationwide impact</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe7371774a96b652607011fe9b8e6d35fc2390674955349b437d71b735d9859a</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:51:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T01:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-s-state-election-will-have-a-nationwide-impact/a-78874569--8cf3f82cd3a7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-s-state-election-will-have-a-nationwide-impact/a-78874569?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The parliamentary election in the small eastern state of Saxony-Anhalt could have dramatic consequences for Germany's federal government, further raising dissatisfaction with Chancellor Friedrich Merz.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>US envoys meet with Putin, leave Russia for Kyiv</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bb2cd809f670951d34fd06b1b97ef58487a830cdf416917127a258c810d29e94</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:51:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T22:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-envoys-meet-with-putin-leave-russia-for-kyiv/a-79040773--6af20c7cc1f8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-envoys-meet-with-putin-leave-russia-for-kyiv/a-79040773?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jared Kushner and Steve Witkoff met with Russian President Vladimir Putin in Moscow to try to revive talks to end the war in Ukraine. The US envoys are also scheduled to visit Kyiv on Sunday.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German company successfully launches rocket to space</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:78adf2cb44cd820823455eda66204561bdfe38fd07513c276c57a30ef66ac2f4</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:51:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T22:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-company-successfully-launches-rocket-to-space/a-79050717--59c961471bc2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-company-successfully-launches-rocket-to-space/a-79050717?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bavaria-based Isar Aerospace managed to launch its Spectrum rocket into orbit, 18 months after its first attempt. This is the first such launch from European soil.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Why many Syrians feel Assad death sentence isn't enough</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dc6f8c3412023b92c6b9eebd204c5d465868e1ee51424ee04c9337fd83dfdba8</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T18:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-many-syrians-feel-assad-death-sentence-isn-t-enough/a-78985915--4ab418802105.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-many-syrians-feel-assad-death-sentence-isn-t-enough/a-78985915?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In July, a Syrian court sentenced former dictator Bashar Assad to death for crimes against his own people. But after 14 years of civil war, many survivors are demanding more when it comes to transitional justice.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Croatia: Toxic waste protest draws tens of thousands</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d890657ac3e2c2d734114d2c493b6d08506c748e2b3b8bace2c0bbdb68a6c9af</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T17:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/croatia-toxic-waste-protest-draws-tens-of-thousands/a-79049228--9dec1bdce80c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/croatia-toxic-waste-protest-draws-tens-of-thousands/a-79049228?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Zagreb demonstrators demanded that the government come up with a plan to clear illegal toxic waste in 20 days. Prime Minister Plenkovic has promised to tackle the issue.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Masked anti-migrant protesters block UK's Dover terminal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d2e239eab4078a4c6e37d23aafb2e2b0b21689f6f1de43f78c8cb3e1c0bd86d2</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T14:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/masked-anti-migrant-protesters-block-uk-s-dover-terminal/a-79046929--f6606768718e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/masked-anti-migrant-protesters-block-uk-s-dover-terminal/a-79046929?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chanting "stop the boats" and wearing balaclavas, the demonstrators blocked traffic at the UK's busiest international ferry port.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: Germany's postal voting system isn't rigged</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b01f5a425fdfc696737e2b1c4f64b4f70c6c8aa4a50a4f6c19033336de63862b</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T13:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-germany-s-postal-voting-system-isn-t-rigged/a-78958438--ffb06136be22.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-germany-s-postal-voting-system-isn-t-rigged/a-78958438?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Germany heads into three elections in September, rumors are circulating on social media claiming that postal voting is not secure — claims that have also been made about other elections. Here's why they're wrong.</summary><category term="German election" /></entry><entry><title>Iran: US hits 3 IRGC-linked oil tankers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:67549143806aadc3ae8932c7d051ee823add5840097d5fddd606ef8d8d718559</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:51:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T08:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-us-hits-3-irgc-linked-oil-tankers/live-79044467--62e9bb33b870.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-us-hits-3-irgc-linked-oil-tankers/live-79044467?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US military said it had destroyed three vessels linked to Iran's Revolutionary Guards. Tehran responded by threatening to increase strikes on US ships in the region.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: From emigration to immigration destination</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:37de42eb13ff2f9ef2c68ba41b09026b6b10842cd38821edaf29830b6ffcc07c</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T08:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-from-emigration-to-immigration-destination/a-78805541--ac3bd047b864.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-from-emigration-to-immigration-destination/a-78805541?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Migration is a sensitive topic in Germany, with public debate dominated by the fear of uncontrolled immigration. But over two centuries, millions of Germans emigrated in search of a better life.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>India news: 275 Indians still missing in Nepal floods</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:de09b59848da8525acf9ed61fa19546dcbc007d2e8ecb5dcfb1a1987f275883f</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T07:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-275-indians-still-missing-in-nepal-floods/live-79043198--94765ec2f3ce.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-275-indians-still-missing-in-nepal-floods/live-79043198?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Official estimates say that 275 Indians continue to be unaccounted for in Nepal's flood catastrophe. Meanwhile, no Indian travelers are said to be stranded in flood-affected Tibet. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Thousands march at Saxony-Anhalt rallies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e3d812954d08d281ed9d92d5ec6ab92f7ec7178d0eef9d5da910210e0167a2c2</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T06:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-thousands-march-at-saxony-anhalt-rallies/live-79041302--28cda5652dc8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-thousands-march-at-saxony-anhalt-rallies/live-79041302?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ahead of Saxony-Anhalt's state election on Sunday, a democracy festival by civil society groups has been held in Magdeburg. The far-right AfD organized its final campaign rally in the state capital.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>What would an AfD government in Saxony-Anhalt really mean?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:685a044eccf3414c616c9105db3dd5f1e626c48e9b8c7bee272c9b30bb1314bc</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T06:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-would-an-afd-government-in-saxony-anhalt-really-mean/a-78869947--261ff10619b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-would-an-afd-government-in-saxony-anhalt-really-mean/a-78869947?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Detention centers for deportation, mandatory work for asylum-seekers, vigilante groups — the AfD wants to drastically overhaul Saxony-Anhalt. What does the party have planned?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Tunisia: Judge orders arrest of journalist Mohamed Yousfi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1f3f8313f1d56882f8019a034f2e47f7fc55d24bf99eae5f7b9c415a06c3f88c</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T03:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tunisia-judge-orders-arrest-of-journalist-mohamed-yousfi/a-79040802--a89422e15909.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tunisia-judge-orders-arrest-of-journalist-mohamed-yousfi/a-79040802?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A journalist and vocal critic of the Tunisian president, Mohamed Yousfi has been taken into custody ahead of an interview. A union called the arrest an attack on all journalists' rights.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bolivia: Deadly explosion rocks military base in Viacha</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:64448fbce88e7c9c8a04d7ac94423e3b569c231ccfff0fe04ba9d96a0a3fc235</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T03:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bolivia-deadly-explosion-rocks-military-base-in-viacha/a-79040892--c627a7e7a20e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bolivia-deadly-explosion-rocks-military-base-in-viacha/a-79040892?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The explosion occurred at an army base where fireworks were stored. The exact cause of the blast is under investigation.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>UN approves world map reflecting true size of Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd093177f6f6e70ed7db9755226067a81c8abd32ae4d7ca0080f1beed0a438c7</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T23:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/un-approves-world-map-reflecting-true-size-of-africa/a-79040629--e6486bc869d9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/un-approves-world-map-reflecting-true-size-of-africa/a-79040629?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The UN General Assembly has voted to adopt a map that more accurately shows the size of the continents. Only the United States voted against the measure, which projects the country as smaller than on traditional maps.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Outrage as Maltese tycoon acquitted in journalist's murder</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2cdc13d509a2ef7d1fbf9ce5882279a7f4679a6cec16529c535b956446c70325</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T19:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/outrage-as-maltese-tycoon-acquitted-in-journalist-s-murder/a-79027008--2a5e65f2e4f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/outrage-as-maltese-tycoon-acquitted-in-journalist-s-murder/a-79027008?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Maltese businessman Yorgen Fenech has been found not guilty of complicity to murder journalist Daphne Caruana Galizia. Almost nine years after the attack, the question of who ordered her death remains unanswered.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen: Fighting intensifies amid Houthi push in the west</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3fe02122a250560ab194d5451f051c8af22ae8f10a8678df8da3b46c9ef4b5b8</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T19:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/yemen-fighting-intensifies-amid-houthi-push-in-the-west/a-79039588--651aa6fc20cf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/yemen-fighting-intensifies-amid-houthi-push-in-the-west/a-79039588?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Houthi forces are trying to secure high ground and solidify their control of the entry to the Red Sea in the southwest. The Iran-backed militia abandoned a shaky truce with the Saudi-backed government-in-exile in July.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>In Saxony-Anhalt election, small parties will be kingmakers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2103c98349bcac1a9cc4ee71568a8363d6ed4651922e4c4caea5a54471c1d677</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T19:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/in-saxony-anhalt-election-small-parties-will-be-kingmakers/a-78482460--43a765f0394e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/in-saxony-anhalt-election-small-parties-will-be-kingmakers/a-78482460?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The far-right AfD has good odds of winning an absolute majority in Saxony-Anhalt's parliament this state election, enabling them to govern alone. It all depends on whether other parties make the cut.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's civil society alliance takes on the far right</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:841b8b4fe086df69c5f7904f1a24203ad73c94dd2c39048257e1c42a37a379ef</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T18:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-civil-society-alliance-takes-on-the-far-right/a-79009105--a9caa6e26042.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-civil-society-alliance-takes-on-the-far-right/a-79009105?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Trade unions, churches and human rights activists are worried about the rise of the far-right AfD. How can civil society protect people who are threatened by far-right extremism?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>How vulnerable is Germany's infrastructure?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa403bf0d746b23a7feb97d2ea16fd36643a93fd2bc7d855f7109bc05eb16c5d</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T13:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-vulnerable-is-germany-s-infrastructure/a-78990131--c453d562d3d7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-vulnerable-is-germany-s-infrastructure/a-78990131?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The growing number of attacks on substations and railway lines in Germany is raising concern. Experts say that people will have to get used to the likelihood that such incidents will continue.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Majority of Germans see Russia as a threat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3215e529ed09e7250e23bd74aee3bbe6cb7b680af3e23ab9f539ab899f1336bc</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T12:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/majority-of-germans-see-russia-as-a-threat/a-78970396--5eab015b811e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/majority-of-germans-see-russia-as-a-threat/a-78970396?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">More than half of German citizens believe that Germany's security is threatened by Russia, according to the latest survey by public broadcaster ARD.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>The hidden environmental cost of AI data centers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fef6864c1f0a05a5dd72da998d06b902feb61765169271ccf7eb4684c09d97a7</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T11:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-hidden-environmental-cost-of-ai-data-centers/a-78789889--5e00024ffa87.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-hidden-environmental-cost-of-ai-data-centers/a-78789889?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As data centers multiply to meet AI demand, they're straining power grids, draining water supplies and reshaping the land and air around them.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia: How the funeral of Ratko Mladic is dividing a nation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1c7ad5c9aedf4c478e7f3d1343573c0a17fb5571d31fc405c371f87fbd86005e</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T11:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-how-the-funeral-of-ratko-mladic-is-dividing-a-nation/a-78948890--47086bf0a8c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-how-the-funeral-of-ratko-mladic-is-dividing-a-nation/a-78948890?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the Serbian government leaves the decision about Ratko Mladic's funeral arrangements to his family, international pressure on the country is mounting. How do Serbs feel about the matter?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Is Saxony-Anhalt's economy really struggling?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:872c8b5d00b2883870a4f9e7dcc4c26e02b62b9b132fcaffb805a36066841918</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T10:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-is-saxony-anhalt-s-economy-really-struggling/a-78867143--acfa7a18352e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-is-saxony-anhalt-s-economy-really-struggling/a-78867143?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's far-right AfD party has long claimed that the eastern state of Saxony-Anhalt has been left behind. Is that really the case? A closer look at the data offers some interesting insights.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Why North Korea's women's football team is so good</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:715d6f7258f8df1a8e1f5c3393de46f9d4fb9f39ae0fa3c5e09e526d6d6d52db</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T10:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-north-korea-s-women-s-football-team-is-so-good/a-70313505--6b31ccb5ebf0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-north-korea-s-women-s-football-team-is-so-good/a-70313505?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">North Korea's young footballers enter the U-20 World Cup in Poland as defending champions — the 2024 title was their third. Why is the isolated state so good at the game?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>2026 Beethoven Festival evokes a sense of home</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1de6fb61cd63bbb001a1a813f88a36100ca9afee5ed7d77fc598ac45fc183651</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T08:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/2026-beethoven-festival-evokes-a-sense-of-home/a-78892997--9bbbc99c220c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/2026-beethoven-festival-evokes-a-sense-of-home/a-78892997?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The motto of this year's classical music festival in Bonn is "Home/At Home," featuring musicians from diverse cultures presenting pieces from their homelands.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>How Volkswagen's huge workforce became a costly burden</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:73f7d61a4b4b55d28b564087441cf8a198e7e0fbaf8cc09ee7282098f4bedd82</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T07:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-volkswagen-s-huge-workforce-became-a-costly-burden/a-77766154--6b1e762393dc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-volkswagen-s-huge-workforce-became-a-costly-burden/a-77766154?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The struggling German carmaker plans to cut up to 100,000 jobs from its 630,000-strong workforce. How did VW's headcount get so bloated, and will the cuts be enough to survive the Chinese EV onslaught?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Berlin: BER Airport Terminal 1 reopened after security scare</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1b5747d8d5f71b285b072c6ee7abdeda2421f3d184b104af0343958d174fd9e6</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T21:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/berlin-ber-airport-terminal-1-evacuated-after-security-scare/a-78895207--c34e813b5301.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/berlin-ber-airport-terminal-1-reopened-after-security-scare/a-78895207?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police have given the all-clear at Terminal 1 at Berlin's BER Airport following an earlier security scare and evacuation. The airport said some flights had been delayed but they were trying to avoid any cancelations.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Norway seizes Russian ship in Svalbard to compensate Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4dd3e3137d2550980ff5bda746d20681d8644f555c55dd6c5f49b010eb7faff4</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T15:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/norway-seizes-russian-ship-in-svalbard-to-compensate-ukraine/a-78889005--08f506bc071c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/norway-seizes-russian-ship-in-svalbard-to-compensate-ukraine/a-78889005?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Authorities in Norway have seized a Russian ship, the Professor Molchanov, on a court order sought and obtained by Naftogaz in Ukraine. Russia has protested the move, which stems from its refusal to pay Naftogaz damages.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Is Germany's economic slump finally over?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:060e39ed183dae8384b7793e16f732fe0f84dc25e3c5d43bae56ecbdab26238c</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T12:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-germany-s-economic-slump-finally-over/a-78815447--a101d614d4d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-germany-s-economic-slump-finally-over/a-78815447?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Despite a slew of negative headlines, the German economy has posted its best figures in years. There are reasons for optimism, but structural issues remain.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Police say arson attack targeted defense firm</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:867ef23b0bf29ff4542461fc3d9f95243aeee201c1d00d293cd3ce8263aedb3c</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T07:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-police-say-arson-attack-targeted-defense-firm/live-78818089--febcbc9ac7c0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-police-say-arson-attack-targeted-defense-firm/live-78818089?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two people were arrested in connection with a small fire at a construction site near a defense tech company in Munich. Investigators are looking at a possible "political motive."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia to close branches of Germany's Goethe-Institut</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ee0154e25774587d6e70e9d25f827abd2c925e6bfa90234f8584ef6ffe10a512</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T03:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-to-close-branches-of-germany-s-goethe-institut/a-78815269--cfadf2790699.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-to-close-branches-of-germany-s-goethe-institut/a-78815269?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russian Foreign Minister Sergey Lavrov said the move was in response to Germany's decision to close the Russian House in Berlin after blaming Moscow for an attempted drone attack at Leipzig/Halle Airport.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: How to woo voters with an immigrant background</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:03d389cdad7511ae74a3d231fe6131180f6a09392475a5048cfe85c573755354</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T16:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-how-to-woo-voters-with-an-immigrant-background/a-78790775--114185b0d97d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-how-to-woo-voters-with-an-immigrant-background/a-78790775?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The number of voters in Germany with an immigrant background is rising. Yet the established parties barely manage to reach them. Why not?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Macron visits Bayeux Tapestry with King Charles, PM Andy Burnham</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8144c3fa4925684f6f85c2533443676191e09fa225ac6cfb9dd6bd8847e1b0e6</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T16:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/macron-visits-bayeux-tapestry-with-king-charles-pm-andy-burnham/a-78772317--2945f5b2dad4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/macron-visits-bayeux-tapestry-with-king-charles-pm-andy-burnham/a-78772317?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron is on a shorter-term visit to the UK than the renowned on-loan 11th century tapestry. He viewed the ancient artwork with the UK monarch and relatively new Prime Minister Andy Burnham.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia's hybrid attacks on Germany: how should Berlin react?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ddb2e95e6e70a38d364edaf37ba515a09d59a2416cc3bb5a40b8cf7e24fb91e5</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T15:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-s-hybrid-attacks-on-germany-how-should-berlin-react/a-78784262--b9b2455adcd2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-s-hybrid-attacks-on-germany-how-should-berlin-react/a-78784262?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany holds Russia responsible for an attempted drone attack on Leipzig airport. But critics say Berlin's response, including the closure of Russia's consulate in Bonn, has been too timid.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Austria women ice hockey team fight for future generations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0619cad458eeede17189c12ae722d19cb813295bfbfd87a972f178341de86d13</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T15:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/austria-women-ice-hockey-team-fight-for-future-generations/a-78771578--3801f62b822d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/austria-women-ice-hockey-team-fight-for-future-generations/a-78771578?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Austria are getting ready for their first Women's Ice Hockey World Championship. But preparations have been overshadowed by a dispute about conditions, pay and getting men's cast-off kit. A solution now looks in sight.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>EU summons Russian envoy over failed Leipzig drone attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6b3e8653a2cb6aa95edebcb027a3fc6b7307385c07fc0587ee53d1b29b29e027</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T08:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-summons-russian-envoy-over-failed-leipzig-drone-attack/a-78687280--4f4b3de05209.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-summons-russian-envoy-over-failed-leipzig-drone-attack/a-78687280?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU's foreign policy chief Kaja Kallas said the attempted attack had "all the hallmarks of state-sponsored terrorism." She said the EU was summoning a Russian envoy, with France announcing a similar step.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Women's football: Anyomi, London City and the German exodus</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:106796ee7d25e6a1a9397b459c541b478cf332854fc6aaa690ba6d6ec43b2358</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T07:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/women-s-football-anyomi-london-city-and-the-german-exodus/a-78446131--1f6d62473b8a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/women-s-football-anyomi-london-city-and-the-german-exodus/a-78446131?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nicole Anyomi has joined Alexia Putellas and other star names in signing for the ambitious English club London City Lionesses. The Germany winger told DW England is a better place to develop her game than back home.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Russia threatens 'devastating' Baltic response</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:45df56530bff6aab550ff62832f149e45f7ae15370a4308b840fbf549527ac4a</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T00:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-threatens-devastating-baltic-response/live-78582421--a061a45930f9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-threatens-devastating-baltic-response/live-78582421?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Any escalation in the Baltic region will lead to a significant response, Moscow said.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany says Russia behind attempted drone attack at Leipzig airport</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8da29d92c8ecc0928289abf6044a5023e400a50096650463eec511a4682c3586</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T22:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-says-russia-behind-attempted-drone-attack-at-leipzig-airport/a-78584589--1b81c9b87e46.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-says-russia-behind-attempted-drone-attack-at-leipzig-airport/a-78584589?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Investigators believe an explosives-laden drone was deliberately targeting a Ukrainian cargo aircraft at Leipzig/Halle airport in early August. The German government said on Tuesday that it held Russia "responsible."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany terminates lease for Berlin's Russian House</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:16ca6cf63c22c43c4e13d161a004976fb868f0247ebcfaf89f33f59f495c082c</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T16:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-terminates-lease-for-berlin-s-russian-house/a-73037945--11d07f6e3f4b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-terminates-lease-for-berlin-s-russian-house/a-73037945?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany has announced the termination of the lease for the Russian House in the heart of Berlin. Critics have long said it is a hub for propaganda and espionage.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Can communities be proteced from melting glaciers?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f3408c1c4502dd036b12c1f33a9ed53fbd009d861d77a1f1c783b93e5c7ffb72</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T13:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-glaciers-melt-can-communities-be-protected/a-78615775--a898d3259825.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-communities-be-proteced-from-melting-glaciers/a-78615775?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rising temperatures are increasing the risk of floods and avalanches in mountain regions. The disaster in Nepal and Tibet shows the urgent need for solutions, and the tools that could help save lives.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Mladic's death, Bosnia and Serbia's unfinished reckoning</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b507609ce13eb9cc88176d6e1fd5fe649890feeb11c9f71c58fc3f1b7ab57dec</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T13:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/mladic-s-death-bosnia-and-serbia-s-unfinished-reckoning/a-78602733--165fe4759bb5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/mladic-s-death-bosnia-and-serbia-s-unfinished-reckoning/a-78602733?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The death of Ratko Mladic did not close a dark chapter of European history; it reopened old wounds. The ideology that created him lives on. The Dayton peace agreement ended the war, not the divisions that produced it.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Norway's new King Haakon VIII takes oath in parliament</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:46460fb5829ab6a194da34e08449ead1053bdf6427f6db60b1adc87876a4b160</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T12:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/norway-s-new-king-haakon-viii-takes-oath-in-parliament/a-78606923--f49dd1cbb150.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/norway-s-new-king-haakon-viii-takes-oath-in-parliament/a-78606923?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The new king swore to uphold the constitution in parliament in Oslo, the first major institutional step of his reign. Haakon VIII's wife Queen Mette-Marit had to skip the event in the aftermath of her lung transplant.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's center-left SPD is fighting for survival</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6ef3d1dbfd404590f08d71939c40ba797415021e1b525943c4b61ce5fc7c63ae</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T11:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-center-left-spd-is-fighting-for-survival/a-78586448--2801e792e220.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-center-left-spd-is-fighting-for-survival/a-78586448?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Social Democratic Party is sinking ever deeper into crisis. Voters are turning away, while unrest is growing within its grassroots ranks. Will upcoming state elections accelerate the party's downward spiral?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>US irks Germany, Europe with Russian G20 invite, press bans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:925ae3325865dccdc066345d423a2b16943a14e5549ac5d973362d1ef19eb63d</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T10:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-irks-germany-europe-with-russian-g20-invite-press-bans/a-78583919--4573442379c3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-irks-germany-europe-with-russian-g20-invite-press-bans/a-78583919?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia's finance minister is at the G20 meeting in Asheville but some key US press corps members are not. The mood was already tense amid the lengthy Iran war and Trump's renewed beef with neighbor Canada.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Can new Apple CEO John Ternus fix the tech giant's AI woes?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5fe1ba89416464a3c8a5fee6a96138a03a77bdacf3e3ecf8159efc2a3c84e152</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T09:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-new-apple-ceo-john-ternus-fix-the-tech-giant-s-ai-woes/a-78575898--ec9f6d3fb1f9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-new-apple-ceo-john-ternus-fix-the-tech-giant-s-ai-woes/a-78575898?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">John Ternus is just the third Apple CEO in 30 years. His primary challenge is to correct the company's faltering AI strategy to preserve its position as a big tech leader.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Ulrich Siegmund wants to make Saxony-Anhalt a model for AfD rule</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b73d33b6966f5b9e33c5d2086606c9901489cb4cb97e929e618c6e697e8c603c</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T04:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ulrich-siegmund-wants-to-make-saxony-anhalt-a-model-for-afd-rule/a-78579499--1e4a7373edd6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ulrich-siegmund-wants-to-make-saxony-anhalt-a-model-for-afd-rule/a-78579499?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The AfD's lead candidate Ulrich Siegmund aims to turn his small federal state into a blueprint for right-wing extremist politics across Germany.</summary><categor