, AI, hardware costs and slowing user growth are putting pressure on the global games industry despite its current strength.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Remembering Dolly Parton: 8 facts about the icon</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:186bbbb8c65a7bca67dff7a84f3c02c8f18e156874838df9e9694d20c1538375</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T18:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/remembering-dolly-parton-8-facts-about-the-icon/a-75503168--5fa1e70ed52f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/remembering-dolly-parton-8-facts-about-the-icon/a-75503168?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Dolly Parton, one of the world's most successful artists, has died at the age of 80. Here are some important and extraordinary facts about the country music superstar.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>US country music legend Dolly Parton dies aged 80</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0d5597785e86397904a179282dedcdf30f7f1ad6112eee13f3c8a5780b05398c</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T18:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-country-music-legend-dolly-parton-dies-aged-80/a-78501931--2eb06224b286.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-country-music-legend-dolly-parton-dies-aged-80/a-78501931?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Representatives of the country music legend told US media that Dolly Parton died after a "brief battle with cancer." Parton's career spans more than half a century and includes a wide array of smash hits.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Grain exports stall as Ukraine steps up attacks on Russia's Black Sea ports</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ce3b4202cbfd87273626a2170f91466eef1acab2f18af664e6fba70dc78f638e</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T18:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/grain-exports-stall-as-ukraine-steps-up-attacks-on-russia-s-black-sea-ports/a-78499629--4f2c24015c22.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/grain-exports-stall-as-ukraine-steps-up-attacks-on-russia-s-black-sea-ports/a-78499629?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian drone strikes on Russian infrastructure on the Black Sea are disrupting grain and oil exports from the port of Novorossiysk and other key hubs.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Schalke coach looks to Bosnia bond in Bundesliga return</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:94e14205e7fd470f622ffbe58034a0a333cf65383e3b6e1a1dcec0dd43d4d165</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T14:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/schalke-coach-looks-to-bosnia-bond-in-bundesliga-return/a-78486008--84b6333f3a23.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/schalke-coach-looks-to-bosnia-bond-in-bundesliga-return/a-78486008?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After three seasons in the second division, Schalke are back in the Bundesliga. Just a year ago, few would have guessed that their revival would largely be 'Made in Bosnia.'</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Can Germany defend itself against drone attacks?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:827f361e5d752bae8b4637bde4a30a42cddbec9aed196c98a679ec8756d9c90c</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T14:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-germany-defend-itself-against-drone-attacks/a-78353414--699e49b4993c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-germany-defend-itself-against-drone-attacks/a-78353414?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Explosive-laden drones at Leipzig/Halle airport have exposed gaps in Germany's defenses. DW looks at how prepared the country is for future drone attacks.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Why Germany's Volkswagen could cut 100,000 jobs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca061e0d8c09a9e09a26c0b40f89f20f2c0a4877775f439f5cb54328d81dab0b</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T13:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-germany-s-volkswagen-could-cut-100-000-jobs/a-78483715--3ad4df2f83bb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-germany-s-volkswagen-could-cut-100-000-jobs/a-78483715?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Europe's biggest automaker, Volkswagen, faces Chinese competition, high costs and US tariffs. What could its restructuring mean for the German car industry?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Can new US sanctions cripple Iran's shadow economy?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d9a8fe826fc79c12b1e1df6a3e66a2faead6e4dbc023562f4a29137b7eacdb2</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T10:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-new-us-sanctions-cripple-iran-s-shadow-economy/a-78494630--d793d396bd52.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-new-us-sanctions-cripple-iran-s-shadow-economy/a-78494630?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US is expanding sanctions on Iran's financial networks, targeting crypto, gold, aviation and shipping. DW spoke with analysts about what could change.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Trees are vital for cooler cities, but they need help too</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:80d5194fcf3ee9db81a59a603f0212971be4b2c49655a014a424df07eff6a34e</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T09:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trees-are-vital-for-cooler-cities-but-they-need-help-too/a-78488665--39588bf2d5df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trees-are-vital-for-cooler-cities-but-they-need-help-too/a-78488665?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Record-breaking heat and drought are putting urban trees at risk. Experts explain how to protect these essential assets and build city forests that can withstand the climate challenges ahead.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>The new Bundesliga season is here, but has the glow gone?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c2ec3c137fcdd262cd88960e8018777df3b454fdcbc3ff0eed21ce975c81b8a</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-24T14:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-new-bundesliga-season-is-here-but-has-the-glow-gone/a-78062032--f578ab52d735.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-new-bundesliga-season-is-here-but-has-the-glow-gone/a-78062032?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Another Bundesliga season arrives, but are the golden years of Germany's top football league already over, and what can it do to change its course?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Star violinist Anne-Sophie Mutter: 50 years on stage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a52dd63affe757ba4d02d2eda9f16e5f518477e6d4df0c82ae9e095301cf4d4a</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-24T11:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/star-violinist-anne-sophie-mutter-50-years-on-stage/a-78484739--30785cb37716.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/star-violinist-anne-sophie-mutter-50-years-on-stage/a-78484739?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Anne-Sophie Mutter constantly reinvents herself. For her 50th onstage anniversary, the star violinist is surprising audiences with sounds from around the world and never-before-recorded commissions.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Scientists discover new 'immune hubs' in skull bone marrow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aad229c1feef2488b411ae99f147337f091e170362bca31abd4c836f68037281</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-24T08:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/scientists-discover-new-immune-hubs-in-skull-bone-marrow/a-78460417--3ae7f2c7a79f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/scientists-discover-new-immune-hubs-in-skull-bone-marrow/a-78460417?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">"Immune hubs" that actively defend the brain have been discovered in mouse skull marrow. Similar cells exist in human skulls, but their role remains unclear.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Spiraling health costs force Iranians to delay care</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6dfc2dd7823bb96ad16677f0c3c5caab0f996ff8d81a1b8f1575d7d64d148e65</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-24T08:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spiraling-health-costs-force-iranians-to-delay-care/a-78455430--f9e115d582df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spiraling-health-costs-force-iranians-to-delay-care/a-78455430?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A single chemotherapy session in Iran can cost six times the monthly minimum wage. As drug prices soar and medicine is in short supply, doctors say more patients are delaying or abandoning treatment.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Could Russia's growing fuel crisis help end the Ukraine war?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:03e367f9fd38ac73c6bbe1fe882375c1f848c94560c8a1c840ec80780efae87e</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-23T14:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/could-russia-s-growing-fuel-crisis-help-end-the-ukraine-war/a-78472138--c1b9534fc17c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/could-russia-s-growing-fuel-crisis-help-end-the-ukraine-war/a-78472138?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian attacks on oil refineries have deepened Russia's fuel crisis, with shortages reaching Moscow. Could growing public anger put Putin under pressure?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Sydney Marathon medal wrongly shows German landmark</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cc655bd2feb40ec8e961b13eb628bdb39b70a3985e9c5c5f113a749666258128</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-23T06:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/sydney-marathon-medal-wrongly-shows-german-landmark/a-78473705--c4d12c38e946.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/sydney-marathon-medal-wrongly-shows-german-landmark/a-78473705?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A medal minted for finishers in the Sydney Marathon features a skyline of the city — with one landmark from rather far away. Organizers say the muddle only makes the medal "a little more unique."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>'Masha and the Bear': Ukraine sanctions Russian cartoon</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:69f051fe9fc262cabc298dd654b161e5f2afc5f8520657f9ade42ac642f54d1d</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-21T18:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/masha-and-the-bear-ukraine-sanctions-russian-cartoon/a-78464406--5a8b6056ca62.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/masha-and-the-bear-ukraine-sanctions-russian-cartoon/a-78464406?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukraine has imposed sanctions on the hit Russian children's cartoon "Masha and the Bear," a step towards banning it. The culture minister called the show propaganda. Russia said the move showed Kyiv's "ugly nature."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bauhaus Manifesto: Broad alliance promoting artistic freedom</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8ad74993829aa8c2f8dac2ea944eeb4fc2958ffb83eb6861bee66a88e028f6a3</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-21T10:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bauhaus-manifesto-broad-alliance-promoting-artistic-freedom/a-78456460--2d3d86ae9554.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bauhaus-manifesto-broad-alliance-promoting-artistic-freedom/a-78456460?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Weeks before Saxony-Anhalt's state election, representatives from German cultural, crafts, architecture, design and church sectors unite to promote freedom, openness and creativity.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Ronaldinho to make football comeback aged 46</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc44ca4c8c8bd39b851c825327f0e33186df600916e894663e0e324f0f29abe6</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-21T08:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ronaldinho-to-make-football-comeback-aged-46/a-78453950--1b84029c6c14.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ronaldinho-to-make-football-comeback-aged-46/a-78453950?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">More than a decade after his last professional appearance, Brazilian superstar Ronaldinho is set for a comeback. The former world player of the year is to play in Italy’s third tier.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Why Germany's gas storage levels are so low</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:410c329f739cda1dc0ade31dda3f25c3d933915ca3d9dd932402a6c41a77482b</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-20T14:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-germany-s-gas-storage-levels-are-so-low/a-78440677--5b5bdc8c00df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-germany-s-gas-storage-levels-are-so-low/a-78440677?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's gas storage facilities are only 50% full as traders bet that wholesale prices will fall if the Iran war ends. With around three months until winter, DW asks whether the country can refill its reserves in time.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>How Europe can better protect against extreme wildfires</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:144b7e0239fd1d7748ef7e2ff91f30350e33b0a91b89c94213d93aebdb74cf6d</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-20T09:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-europe-can-better-protect-against-extreme-wildfires/a-78435243--a1a3032b9e1f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-europe-can-better-protect-against-extreme-wildfires/a-78435243?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In another summer of European wildfires that have even seen wetlands burning, scientists say the situation is set to worsen in the future. What's needed is fire prevention and climate protection.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Bernadette Amani 'living her dream' at Bayern Munich</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2f071ce9a531527e192be5f2ea1b7ba38ef782be1e5da825aa2a1892d457097f</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-20T08:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bernadette-amani-living-her-dream-at-bayern-munich/a-78141213--b6c7f9815814.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bernadette-amani-living-her-dream-at-bayern-munich/a-78141213?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bernadette Amani is heading into her first full season with Bayern Munich, having joined the club in January. Making a living at football is something she never imagined possible while growing up in rural Ivory Coast.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Evergrande founder Hui Ka Yan sentenced to life in prison</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:03d06af47f122ca27ead9918f2ba84aab9dcd597f6db1b549f725639aad0a8ee</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-20T07:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/evergrande-founder-hui-ka-yan-sentenced-to-life-in-prison/a-78439153--ba088f0f4c18.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/evergrande-founder-hui-ka-yan-sentenced-to-life-in-prison/a-78439153?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Chinese court ordered the former billionaire's assets to be confiscated and fined Evergrande-related companies billions of dollars.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bayern Munich's Jamal Musiala collapses on pitch again</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:953ca6388bec4490c435ce957dd7a2c852aab944af87bbacc0af6dcd2dae7396</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-19T10:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-s-jamal-musiala-collapses-on-pitch-again/a-78426021--80b4bb68cef0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-s-jamal-musiala-collapses-on-pitch-again/a-78426021?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">One of Germany's top footballers has collapsed on the pitch for a second time in four days ahead of the new season. Bayern Munich's Jamal Musiala has said he has a "neurological dysfunction" that causes blackouts.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Who really owns the Caspian Sea?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0018a1f5a35cb31af6619a4de28736fd7e39035129018d43c4427e34cdc7da01</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-19T09:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/who-really-owns-the-caspian-sea/a-78396946--815c4887a22c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/who-really-owns-the-caspian-sea/a-78396946?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Five countries border the Caspian Sea, but none owns a fixed share. A 2018 convention established rules for navigation, security and fishing while leaving some seabed borders unresolved.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Messi retirement hint highlights football era nearing an end</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:36a71484874259e7dddb2191881de86ed02718d4e511757ab6a5aef5007f6ce7</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-19T08:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/messi-retirement-hint-highlights-football-era-nearing-an-end/a-78415527--f2918eb8eee5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/messi-retirement-hint-highlights-football-era-nearing-an-end/a-78415527?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Soon after propelling Argentina to a second consecutive World Cup final, Lionel Messi has cast some doubt on his future. While retirement doesn't seem imminent, it still beckons for him and Cristiano Ronaldo.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>In drought-stricken France, tankers supply drinking water</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:15c90cb406b621946b812ace10f1c4194a9bc9d9921665cd362c7e2e5f1e4fe9</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-19T04:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/in-drought-stricken-france-tankers-supply-drinking-water/a-78420016--bd4077809bc7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/in-drought-stricken-france-tankers-supply-drinking-water/a-78420016?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">France is seeing water shortages in regions that usually have plenty of supply. This summer's extreme heat is exposing how unprepared much of the country, and Europe, is for increasing water scarcity.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Will Germany's drought push up food prices?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:87351e693eff170c4e32df490e3abb4d7a3dd46ce2e81064e16e3fe9e3ce5599</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-18T14:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-germany-s-drought-push-up-food-prices/a-78408203--1f8c5e8778fa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-germany-s-drought-push-up-food-prices/a-78408203?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's main farmers' association has warned of a below-average harvest after drought and crops damaged by extreme heat. DW looks into what lower yields could mean for food prices and grocery bills.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Dressed for power: Giorgia Meloni and the language of fashion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:504f810162d86b221974c01def865ef8729095cf79df34825c9a695de11c7a74</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-18T14:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dressed-for-power-giorgia-meloni-and-the-language-of-fashion/a-78413559--c708abdeeebc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dressed-for-power-giorgia-meloni-and-the-language-of-fashion/a-78413559?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From Giorgia Meloni's shift from dark suits to pastels to Angela Merkel's signature jackets, politicians have long used clothing to shape how voters see them. In this day and age, power dressing has evolved.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>How to grow food for more people in a hotter world</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:50f32171e261efab0fb5d0c3d7d95fe7d4996f5e63cce7ed51ed8db1f3f76b98</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-18T13:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-to-grow-food-for-more-people-in-a-hotter-world/a-78413324--6e9042895db0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-to-grow-food-for-more-people-in-a-hotter-world/a-78413324?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Inside futuristic labs, plants are scanned, stressed and analyzed. The aim is to use the results to produce plant strains that can better serve a growing population in a warming world.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>How Germany's Hyrox became a global fitness craze</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:14c0dacbe620d6a3eda472ab4b19bac4ea5dd2adb66db44dc4bb15bc2f3ddcd7</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-18T09:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-germany-s-hyrox-became-a-global-fitness-craze/a-78074218--d75cba260312.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-germany-s-hyrox-became-a-global-fitness-craze/a-78074218?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Created in Germany and now a global success, Hyrox combines running and functional training into a unique format. How a German concept became an international sports phenomenon.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Do not inhale! How wildfire smoke 'affects the whole body'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6e8dc852957d496ce7d2533246b4e1e2bbdfcd13be0c9be3419b3b5a1e455cb3</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-18T08:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/do-not-inhale-how-wildfire-smoke-affects-the-whole-body/a-76039654--04a98638c5fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/do-not-inhale-how-wildfire-smoke-affects-the-whole-body/a-76039654?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Wildfires destroy lives and livelihoods. But survivors and firefighters also suffer long-term harm to their health. A growing body of research suggests particulate matter (PM2.5) in wildfire smoke is a major culprit.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Norway wealth fund sounds alarm on AI stock market bubble</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6026d8199fc6eeacb4a32921219ec2b1a54082eb707b398f6d733b750fc1d679</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-17T14:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/norway-wealth-fund-sounds-alarm-on-ai-stock-market-bubble/a-78351371--685600a6d47d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/norway-wealth-fund-sounds-alarm-on-ai-stock-market-bubble/a-78351371?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The head of Norway's sovereign wealth fund has warned that soaring AI-driven stock valuations could trigger a sharp correction. How exposed is the world's largest sovereign wealth fund to a market downturn?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Can the cool north handle a surge in climate tourism?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:48d7f60f9b546d3573973740e52ea0275597cb1a37278e68b820d79a1c8f3541</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-17T11:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-the-cool-north-handle-a-surge-in-climate-tourism/a-78362462--18cb3d6fa134.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-the-cool-north-handle-a-surge-in-climate-tourism/a-78362462?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With heat records continually being broken and southern summers getting hotter, travelers are heading north. Fragile ecosystems are paying the price.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Fatty food raises risk of colorectal cancer</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:688519c6925a55649d89dccf9a4c7f4c74ad5636207a89133015956ee0b0e6f3</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-17T06:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fatty-food-raises-risk-of-colorectal-cancer/a-78284704--78a75758e125.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fatty-food-raises-risk-of-colorectal-cancer/a-78284704?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Did you know fatty foods can increase production of an acid in your gut that promotes tumor growth? That's on top of all the other health risks linked to fatty foods, like fries and burgers.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Why women are breaking men's endurance records</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:18a9daee6908a3508641581c228b7de8544106991876404b09a245b05512b101</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-14T09:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-women-are-breaking-men-s-endurance-records/a-78362321--f787f66106e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-women-are-breaking-men-s-endurance-records/a-78362321?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Sophie Woods has completed the 2,000-kilometer Via Alpina faster even than the fastest-ever man. DW explains why she is not the only woman breaking men's records in extreme sports.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Hunger stones: The history behind 'if you see me, weep'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b5c6fc36402db775377a825eb2a27788801675068cfbc3dfb6ef3baa82319361</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-14T07:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hunger-stones-the-history-behind-if-you-see-me-weep/a-78345729--34d8ccc8292a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hunger-stones-the-history-behind-if-you-see-me-weep/a-78345729?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Centuries-old hunger stones are emerging as Europe's rivers recede. Among the most famous is the Decin hunger stone in the Elbe River with its cryptic message.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Can a drug help prevent trauma? Study with mice suggests so</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:23612ea3e45ca648e06525b5ead625e261a6237867ca18cad0030b7749b77d10</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-14T06:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-a-drug-help-prevent-trauma-study-with-mice-suggests-so/a-78301961--0a25b16be584.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-a-drug-help-prevent-trauma-study-with-mice-suggests-so/a-78301961?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Researchers in Munich and Stockholm blocked the lifelong social cost of early adversity in mice with a single compound. The catch: it only worked when given during the trauma, not after.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Can we go green without forever chemicals?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c83de73a86fb2e41db851db17b2aa13cfd6b3f8c047fda129b5d8559124d631e</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-13T07:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-we-go-green-without-forever-chemicals/a-77888704--5cf595a2a5e7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-we-go-green-without-forever-chemicals/a-77888704?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As nations globally move to ban forever chemicals, should renewable energy technologies be exempt for the sake of saving the climate?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Eurovision bars countries at war from hosting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae5b0dfcb470fd9d3cf9df89ea590f9477a69a0c89a659463331c1445416b4b4</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-12T18:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eurovision-bars-countries-at-war-from-hosting/a-78341915--0c283d70de4e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eurovision-bars-countries-at-war-from-hosting/a-78341915?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Eurovision victory will no longer guarantee hosting rights if war or a wider security crisis affects the winning country. The change could have particular significance for recent high-flyers Ukraine and Israel.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Mozart tribute ends on sour note after mass figurine theft</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5027193c603cefa7d9971f733cf9c36c7e28c5f4472ad4daee895e83f41d62f0</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-12T16:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/mozart-tribute-ends-on-sour-note-after-mass-figurine-theft/a-78341647--5357f5e2d579.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/mozart-tribute-ends-on-sour-note-after-mass-figurine-theft/a-78341647?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A playful tribute to Mozart has turned into a whodunit after 210 gold-colored figures disappeared from one of Austria's busiest tourist spots. The mass theft forced organizers to end the outdoor display early.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU waste packaging rules: Why small businesses are worried</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da939a0ce72469ecf7db7062733779a3b2a59961d08108d21a75d08307af021a</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-12T09:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-waste-packaging-rules-why-small-businesses-are-worried/a-78326555--4758d7b19395.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-waste-packaging-rules-why-small-businesses-are-worried/a-78326555?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU has introduced new rules targeting packaging waste and "forever chemicals." Although the changes will be phased in slowly, some small sellers have already paused shipments due to the additional red tape.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>AI helping create popular mobile sports games</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:913874cb71dc601178afeb77fd6628ad44ed8f4de08dfca37216c99ef441c6e6</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-12T09:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ai-helping-create-popular-mobile-sports-games/a-78229226--c5ddee08c15c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ai-helping-create-popular-mobile-sports-games/a-78229226?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After the World Cup and before the domestic season, many fans still crave more football. Amateur coders are helping to fill this gap.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Solar eclipse: What to look forward to</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c4174990a9a574a9dee46419b31835f220e5db5cf25db98eba7eb3d14f88061e</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-12T07:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/solar-eclipse-what-to-look-forward-to/a-78330594--591cb72e69ae.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/solar-eclipse-what-to-look-forward-to/a-78330594?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The last solar eclipse visible from the European mainland was in 1999. Here's what to expect, and how to prepare for this rare occasion.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Making sense of Trump's executive order on US vaccinations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f5b310befe228c2aa924eda73722c3b7d66d73aa6fd74fdd7cf6c05e1765b51</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-11T15:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/making-sense-of-trump-s-executive-order-on-us-vaccinations/a-78321723--93af87101bd5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/making-sense-of-trump-s-executive-order-on-us-vaccinations/a-78321723?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump and his Health Secretary Robert F. Kennedy Jr. have long tried to reduce the number of vaccinations available to the US public and even farm animals. The latest move in context.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>How one German city plans to challenge climate extremes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:156bbe983a6590f9935dc5810c862aea05e5786fb0f413c9fbcd60f83d36c320</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-11T07:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-one-german-city-plans-to-challenge-climate-extremes/a-78278373--b05b98bfdb8c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-one-german-city-plans-to-challenge-climate-extremes/a-78278373?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Western Europe has recorded its hottest-ever June and July, and extreme weather from drought to storms is here to stay. How can we adapt to a fundamentally altered climate? Cities like Kiel are trying new ideas.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>How the Rhine drought threatens Germany's economic recovery</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c4d0e26b867590a73a5326c1ad01eed9cc856aa3b3c88ba968000f9f575f9b22</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-10T15:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-the-rhine-drought-threatens-germany-s-economic-recovery/a-78300076--3aa1de887ea7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-the-rhine-drought-threatens-germany-s-economic-recovery/a-78300076?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's inland waterways still move around 5% of the nation's goods. With the Rhine at a critically low level, DW explores how the drought is hitting the economy where it hurts most.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>UEFA, other football federations unite against Infantino</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a806540b0ac8e46af33a3c94621477b2592f5f4a487076c272c6118312a306d2</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-10T11:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uefa-other-football-federations-unite-against-infantino/a-78301601--e313c442a148.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uefa-other-football-federations-unite-against-infantino/a-78301601?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A few weeks ago, Gianni Infantino looked set for another unopposed term as FIFA president. Now, with an election looming, the beleagured football executive is counting the numbers and could be hanging by a thread.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Type 2 diabetes in young women increasingly common</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1b52e14f73bdccbe4252b2e442cd33015fb65d5985068cc8c7c594523fdb048c</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-10T06:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/type-2-diabetes-in-young-women-increasingly-common/a-78251712--f4920d55bd53.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/type-2-diabetes-in-young-women-increasingly-common/a-78251712?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">British researchers say rates of type 2 diabetes are growing most among women under 40. The disease is often underdiagnosed in women or diagnosed too late to reverse the condition's progression.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Study: Obesity 'bigger cancer risk' than previously thought</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f265c43a2f33347f51536616f13d09c464434bdaf60e8ace8d822f9c69f8ab52</id><updated>2026-09-06T04:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-09T09:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/study-obesity-bigger-cancer-risk-than-previously-thought/a-78291063--3902cce5a489.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/study-obesity-bigger-cancer-risk-than-previously-thought/a-78291063?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new study has found that being significantly overweight could be responsible for more cases of cancer than previously known. Abdominal fat, in particular, increases the risk of cancer — especially among women.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry></feed>
